※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4938 LANG_DELEGATED_VALUE_NOT_A_CALL

※ What `yield ⇉` comes to is what the generator it is handed answers when it
※ ends, and only a call of one hands it the walk in one step, with an answer to
※ read.  A walk held in a name is walked through calls, and gives its turns and
※ nothing else.

let std := ⎕import("std")

fn counted() ⇉ u8 → u8:
    yield 1u8
    7u8

fn summed() ⇉ u8:
    let walk := counted()
    let n: u8 = yield ⇉ walk
    yield n

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let total: mut u8 = 0u8
    foreach one := summed():
        total ← total + one
    if total = 8u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
